WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.970 --> 00:00:04.850
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:04.850 --> 00:00:06.970
Today I'm going to
show you how to get

00:00:06.970 --> 00:00:10.090
started using Brocade vADC
products in Google Cloud

00:00:10.090 --> 00:00:11.330
Launcher.

00:00:11.330 --> 00:00:15.070
In Cloud Launcher, search
using the keyword Brocade.

00:00:15.070 --> 00:00:18.533
Multiple offerings of either
the vTM, WAF, or the bundle

00:00:18.533 --> 00:00:19.790
are shown.

00:00:19.790 --> 00:00:23.040
Click on a standard vTM
and vWAF as an example,

00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:26.680
and click on the Launch on
Google Cloud Platform button.

00:00:26.680 --> 00:00:31.130
Select an existing project,
or Create New Project.

00:00:31.130 --> 00:00:33.050
Click on Continue.

00:00:33.050 --> 00:00:37.580
Leave the Name, Zone, Computer
Resources, and Firewall Rules

00:00:37.580 --> 00:00:40.570
as defaults, or
change them as needed.

00:00:40.570 --> 00:00:43.350
Click on Create to
create the instance.

00:00:43.350 --> 00:00:46.940
Once the instance is created,
click on the instance name

00:00:46.940 --> 00:00:49.880
on the VM Instances page.

00:00:49.880 --> 00:00:55.720
Scroll all the way down, and
click on Serial Console Output.

00:00:55.720 --> 00:01:00.880
Again, scroll down to see
the generated password.

00:01:00.880 --> 00:01:03.790
In the VM Instances
page, click on Admin

00:01:03.790 --> 00:01:08.330
Address to configure the vTM,
and use the generated password.

00:01:08.330 --> 00:01:11.900
To get started with Brocade
vADC on Cloud Launcher, click

00:01:11.900 --> 00:01:13.460
on the link in the comments.

00:01:13.460 --> 00:01:15.480
Thanks for watching.

